biokids (1.5.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * BioKids 1.5.0: the packages, from the project's own APT repository.
    Numbered by the rounds it took: 1.0 was the release candidate built as
    0.1.0-2, and five rounds of the owner's tests followed (D-219). The
    ISO comes after (D-185).
  * biokids-shell ships the BioKids browser extension's source; its
    postinst packs and signs it with a key made on the machine
    (biokids-admin pack-extension), and the daemon force-installs it. A
    blocked site opens the launcher's own page, and visited sites are
    recorded by host name only (D-187).
  * One launcher port per child, 7879 + uid % 100, closed to every other
    uid by nftables (D-188).
  * Records are deleted on a schedule set in [retention] of
    /etc/biokids/config.toml (D-189).
  * biokids-ai: biokids-wiki.service and biokids-wiki.path serve the
    offline Wikipedia on 127.0.0.1:7877 once it is downloaded (D-190);
    purge deletes the downloaded models.
  * biokids-panel: biokids-unprovision@.service removes a child from
    BioKids and leaves the account and its home (D-191); a history screen
    (D-192); limits per kind of app (D-193).
  * The AI screen watcher, voice cloning and ElevenLabs are cut (D-180,
    D-181); migration c41d8e0f5a92 drops their columns and table.
  * Logs go to the journal: /var/log/biokids and
    /etc/logrotate.d/biokids-core are removed (D-183).
  * The virtual-terminal guards move to /usr/lib/systemd/logind.conf.d/
    and /usr/share/X11/xorg.conf.d/; the old conffiles in /etc are removed
    on upgrade.
  * The browser policy is removed on "remove", not only on purge.
  * Security fixes from the 2026-10-06 review (D-171), and a daemon
    watchdog, filter checks and verified locks (D-172).
  * Requests answered from the panel, the parent's own recorded voice,
    read-aloud for pre-readers, day schedules, mail to the parent and an
    encyclopedia for the assistant (D-173 to D-178).
  * A guided first run (D-195): the setup wizard opens as soon as the
    packages are installed, a panel shortcut goes on the parent's desktop,
    phone access is four numbered steps, Today offers the one restart setup
    needs, and a help page answers the first questions.
  * biokids-voice: biokids-voice-setup.service downloads Piper and its
    Turkish voice when a parent presses "Doğal sesi indir" in the panel,
    each file checked against a pinned SHA-256 (D-196). Never enabled,
    never started by apt; purging biokids-core with the family's data
    removes what it installed.
  * biokids-shell: the app bar (D-197) - home, the app's own volume and a
    close that stops an app which will not close, at the screen's top
    right over every app. New Depends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
    gir1.2-wnck-3.0, pulseaudio-utils.
  * "Sor Bana" shows only when the assistant can answer, and the daemon
    reaches the assistant's socket through the biokids-ai group (D-198).
    The launcher's sound is two buttons at the top right; "Tablo" leaves
    the catalogue (D-199).
  * biokids-desktop hides the GRUB menu (Esc shows it; removed with the
    package) (D-200).
  * biokids-shell: the app bar leaves a dragged window and comes back on
    its title bar when it stops, re-maximising one dragged out of
    maximisation; a volume slider, the minutes left and the clock; the
    launcher's sound bar can be dragged and its footer lists the apps open
    in the background (D-201).
  * The launcher shows "Bugünün sürprizi", a card that changes every day,
    from a corpus shipped in biokids-core. Dünya is the Marble globe instead
    of Google Earth, which needs WebGL; biokids-desktop now also recommends
    marble, kgeography, kbruch, blinken, ktuberling, palapeli, kturtle and
    gnome-chess (D-203).
  * A search for a word on BioKids' list is never sent (D-202): the
    extension (1.1.0) installs declarativeNetRequest rules from the
    launcher's GET /search-rules, the child sees "Bunu arayamayız", and a
    parent adds the family's own words under Çocuklar > İnternet >
    Gelişmiş. The address bar searches SafeSearch Google without
    suggestions.
  * The launcher's forms ("Büyüğüme sor", "Biraz daha süre iste",
    "Evet, kapat") were refused as forged and showed a blank page: the
    pages asked for no referrer, so Chromium sent "Origin: null". In the
    browser, "Geri dön" goes to the child's start page, a refused search
    reaches the launcher's page even while the browser starts (extension
    1.2.1), and no sign-in invitation is shown (D-204).
  * biokids-shell: the app bar fits the window under it - the whole bar
    from 1000 pixels, a compact one below that, home and close alone under
    520 - and maximises again a new window its app shrinks back (D-205).
  * biokids-panel: an insights screen, "Analiz", for this week, last week
    or the last 30 days in a few plain sentences and server-drawn bars;
    Today gets a "Bu hafta" card and the Sunday mail the same highlights
    (D-206). biokids-core: migration 077ca4545f23 adds usage_hour, screen
    time per hour of the day, kept for activity_days.
  * biokids-panel: an app an upgrade adds is marked "Yeni" for thirty days,
    with one line naming those that suit the child and are not ticked yet
    (D-207).
  * biokids-shell: a tap shows its tile opening until the app's window is
    in front, with no loading screen in between; an app is started once
    however often its tile is tapped; the running app bar brings an open
    app back over $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/biokids-appbar.sock (D-208).
  * biokids-daemon, biokids-shell: "Kapat" is answered at once and the
    computer switches off a few seconds later; with someone else at the
    machine only the child's session ends, and an ssh login does not count
    as someone. The panel's power buttons answer at once too (D-209).
  * biokids-core, biokids-shell: KDiamond ("Elmaslar") and Chrome Music Lab
    ("Müzik Atölyesi") in the catalogue; rows of tiles are centred;
    biokids-desktop recommends kdiamond and tuxpaint-stamps-default (D-210).
  * biokids-panel: no "coming soon" card in Settings.
  * biokids-shell: a sticker album for days spent learning (D-211);
    Resimlerim, the child's own pictures (D-212); three more weekly
    themes (D-213).
  * The evening's end is bedtime: night words, a calm screen and gentle
    dimming (D-214). Special days from Today and holidays on the time
    screen; migration 5d2f8a61c3e4 and the day_changed operation (D-215).
  * biokids-ai: the assistant's answer arrives a sentence at a time, each
    checked before it is shown (D-216).
  * Text size, high contrast and a reading font; biokids-desktop recommends
    fonts-opendyslexic (D-217). A second parent with their own PIN;
    biokids-admin reset-pin --parent; migration b7e41d2c9a63 (D-218).
  * biokids-admin reset-passphrase sets a forgotten family passphrase
    again (D-220).

 -- Bilal Gurkan Sanli <bilalsanli129@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300

biokids (0.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of BioGuard: biokids-core, biokids-daemon,
    biokids-panel, biokids-shell, biokids-voice, the biokids and
    biokids-desktop metapackages, the optional biokids-ai worker, and
    biokids-archive-keyring.
  * Phase 0 scope only. Time accounting, enforcement, the parent panel and
    the child launcher are the product; filtering, earned time, categories
    and the screen watcher ship as packages but are not finished features.
  * The distribution is "trixie" because that is the suite name of the
    project's own archive, which is where these packages are published.
    They are not uploaded to Debian.

 -- Bilal Gurkan Sanli <bilalsanli129@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
